    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 223</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_223/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 04 May 2025 15:50:53 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_223/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Consider the following 3 lines of code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;// 32-bit machine&#xA;1）var x int32 = 32.0&#xA;2）var y int = x&#xA;3）var z rune = x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Will they compile? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If asked this question in an interview, you need to consider what the interviewer wants to test you on.&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h1 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;numeric-literals&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Numeric Literals&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#numeric-literals&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Go, literals are untyped. What does untyped mean? Untyped means they can be assigned to variables or constants of similar types. In the example above, &lt;code&gt;32.0&lt;/code&gt; is an untyped floating-point literal, so it can be assigned to any numeric type variable (or constant). All of the following are legal:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 211</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_211/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 12 Mar 2025 01:16:28 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_211/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Go101 author published an interesting problem that primarily tests subtle details, a characteristic for which the book Go101 is well-known. Let&amp;rsquo;s look at this problem: what is the output of the following program? (Single choice)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;const s = &amp;#34;Go101.org&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;// len(s) == 9&#xA;// 1 &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 9 == 512&#xA;// 512 / 128 == 4&#xA;&#xA;var a byte = 1 &amp;lt;&amp;lt; len(s) / 128&#xA;var b byte = 1 &amp;lt;&amp;lt; len(s[:]) / 128&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    println(a, b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A、0 0&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B、0 4&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C：4 0&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D：4 4&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;There are 2 key points here:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 175</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_175/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jan 2025 10:15:27 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_175/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;const (&#xA;    a = iota&#xA;    b = iota&#xA;)&#xA;const (&#xA;    name = &amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&#xA;    c    = iota&#xA;    d    = iota&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    fmt.Println(a)&#xA;    fmt.Println(b)&#xA;    fmt.Println(c)&#xA;    fmt.Println(d)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;0&#xA;1&#xA;1&#xA;2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/3owhzDo5QeG&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;first-const-block&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;First &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#first-const-block&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;a = iota&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; starts counting from &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; in a &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block, so &lt;code&gt;a = 0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;b = iota&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; increments to &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;b = 1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;second-const-block&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Second &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#second-const-block&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;name = &amp;quot;name&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is not used, but &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s initial value is &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;, and it increments to &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt; after declaration.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;c = iota&lt;/code&gt;: The current &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; value is &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;c = 1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;d = iota&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; continues to increment to &lt;code&gt;2&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;d = 2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;key-rules&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Key Rules&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#key-rules&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; starts counting from &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; in each &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Each line of constant declaration (whether &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is used or not) increments &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; by &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; in different &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; blocks are independent of each other.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 171</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_171/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 25 Jan 2025 23:19:23 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_171/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var ans float64 = 15 &amp;#43; 25 &amp;#43; 5.2&#xA;    fmt.Println(ans)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A: Cannot compile;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B: 45;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C: 45.2;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D: 45.0&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;C&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/VCR1yAY32nG&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;analysis&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Analysis&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#analysis&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;1-constant-expressions&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;1. Constant Expressions&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#1-constant-expressions&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;constant expression&lt;/strong&gt; is an expression that contains only constant operands and is evaluated at compile time.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Constants can be:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Untyped constants&lt;/strong&gt;: e.g., &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;2&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;5.2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typed constants&lt;/strong&gt;: e.g., &lt;code&gt;const b int8 = 3&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Literal constants&lt;/strong&gt;: e.g., &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;2&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;5.2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Named constants&lt;/strong&gt;: e.g., &lt;code&gt;const a = 1 + 2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;2-default-types-of-untyped-constants&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;2. Default Types of Untyped Constants&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#2-default-types-of-untyped-constants&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Although untyped constants do not have an explicit type, they have a default type:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Integer literals (e.g., &lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;25&lt;/code&gt;) have a default type of &lt;code&gt;int&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Floating-point literals (e.g., &lt;code&gt;5.2&lt;/code&gt;) have a default type of &lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;String literals have a default type of &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Boolean literals have a default type of &lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Complex literals have a default type of &lt;code&gt;complex128&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;3-type-inference&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;3. Type Inference&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#3-type-inference&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Go language supports type inference. If the context does not specify an explicit type, the compiler will treat untyped constants as their default type.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;In a constant expression, if the operands include untyped constants of different types, the result&amp;rsquo;s type will be inferred according to the following precedence:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Integer &amp;lt; rune &amp;lt; float &amp;lt; complex.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;4-constant-expression-in-the-problem&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;4. Constant Expression in the Problem&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#4-constant-expression-in-the-problem&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;var ans float64 = 15 &amp;#43; 25 &amp;#43; 5.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;25&lt;/code&gt; are untyped integer constants, with a default type of &lt;code&gt;int&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;5.2&lt;/code&gt; is an untyped floating-point constant, with a default type of &lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;In the constant expression, since &lt;code&gt;5.2&lt;/code&gt; is a floating-point constant, the entire expression&amp;rsquo;s result will be inferred as a floating-point type (&lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;operation-process&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Operation Process&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#operation-process&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The result of &lt;code&gt;15 + 25&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;40&lt;/code&gt;, which is still an untyped integer constant.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The result of &lt;code&gt;40 + 5.2&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;45.2&lt;/code&gt;. Since &lt;code&gt;5.2&lt;/code&gt; is a floating-point constant, the entire expression&amp;rsquo;s result is inferred as &lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;assignment-and-output&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Assignment and Output&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#assignment-and-output&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The final result &lt;code&gt;45.2&lt;/code&gt; is assigned to the variable &lt;code&gt;ans&lt;/code&gt;, whose type is &lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;fmt.Println(ans)&lt;/code&gt; outputs &lt;code&gt;45.2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 160</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_160/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 13 Jan 2025 12:22:18 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_160/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will they compile? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;// 32-bit machine&#xA;1）var x int32 = 32.&#xA;2）var y int = x&#xA;3）var z rune = x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;1 &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/9eGpGYkcqqp&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Can compile&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;2 &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/L5LsYs4NvDO&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Cannot compile&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;3 &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/xgIjiu6PQ1l&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Can compile&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;analysis&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Analysis&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#analysis&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h1 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;go-language-type-system-and-code-analysis&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Go Language Type System and Code Analysis&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#go-language-type-system-and-code-analysis&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;1-untyped-literals&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;1. Untyped Literals&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#1-untyped-literals&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Go, literals (such as &lt;code&gt;32.0&lt;/code&gt;) are untyped. Untyped literals can be implicitly inferred to the target type based on context.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 134</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_134/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 17 Dec 2024 14:00:22 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_134/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {  &#xA;    a := 5&#xA;    b := 8.1&#xA;    fmt.Println(a &amp;#43; b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A.13.1&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B.13&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C.compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: C. Run online: &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/VDTgpXoukTb&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;https://go.dev/play/p/VDTgpXoukTb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Go, there is no implicit type conversion between variables. However, the compiler can perform implicit type conversion between variables and constants.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the problem, &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt; is an &lt;code&gt;int&lt;/code&gt; variable and &lt;code&gt;b&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt; variable.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 125</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_125/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Dec 2024 21:11:41 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_125/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Today, here are two similar problems; note that more than half of people might get them wrong!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Problem 1:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var a int8 = -1&#xA;    var b int8 = -128 / a&#xA;&#xA;    println(b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Problem 2:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    const a int8 = -1&#xA;    var b int8 = -128 / a&#xA;&#xA;    println(b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Will the above two problems compile? If they compile, what will be the output?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 091</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_091/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:18 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_091/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;const (&#xA;    a = iota&#xA;    b = iota&#xA;)&#xA;const (&#xA;    name = &amp;#34;name&amp;#34;&#xA;    c    = iota&#xA;    d    = iota&#xA;)&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    fmt.Println(a)&#xA;    fmt.Println(b)&#xA;    fmt.Println(c)&#xA;    fmt.Println(d)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Reference Answer and Analysis: 0 1 1 2.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Key takeaway: Usage of iota.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is Go language&amp;rsquo;s constant counter, and can only be used in constant expressions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is reset to 0 when the &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; keyword appears, and each new line of constant declaration in a &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block increments &lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; by one.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 081</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_081/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:06 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_081/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var ans float64 = 15 &amp;#43; 25 &amp;#43; 5.2&#xA;    fmt.Println(ans)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A: Cannot compile; B: 45; C: 45.2; D: 45.0&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;C&#xA;Numbers are untyped constants.&#xA;Or rather, they are arbitrary types.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 033</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_033/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:09 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_033/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Today, here are two similar problems; note that more than half of people might get them wrong!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var a int8 = -1&#xA;    var b int8 = -128 / a&#xA;&#xA;    println(b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    const a int8 = -1&#xA;    var b int8 = -128 / a&#xA;&#xA;    println(b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Problem 1:&#xA;Because &lt;code&gt;var b int8 = -128 / a&lt;/code&gt; is not a constant expression, the untyped constant -128 is implicitly converted to &lt;code&gt;int8&lt;/code&gt; type (i.e., the same type as &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt;). Therefore, the result of &lt;code&gt;-128 / a&lt;/code&gt; is of &lt;code&gt;int8&lt;/code&gt; type, and its value is 128, which is outside the range of &lt;code&gt;int8&lt;/code&gt;. Since the result is not a constant, overflow is allowed. The binary representation of 128 is 10000000, which is exactly the two&amp;rsquo;s complement of -128. So, the result of the first problem is -128.&#xA;Problem 2:&#xA;-128 and -1 are both &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;s and are evaluated directly at compile time. The untyped -128 is implicitly converted to &lt;code&gt;int8&lt;/code&gt;, and the result is 128, which is still a &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;. Constant conversion does not allow overflow, leading to a compilation error. The real difference lies in the value of the expression: Problem 1 is not a constant, while Problem 2 is. Constant type conversion does not allow overflow followed by truncation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 028</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_028/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 19:49:55 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_028/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile? If so, what will be the output?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;const (&#xA;    x = iota&#xA;    _&#xA;    y&#xA;    z = &amp;#34;zz&amp;#34;&#xA;    k &#xA;    p = iota&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main()  {&#xA;    fmt.Println(x,y,z,k,p)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Reference Answer: Compiles and outputs: 0 2 zz zz 5&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When defining &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;, if a variable is not followed by a value, it will use the value of the previous variable.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;const (&#xA;    x = iota&#xA;    _ = iota&#xA;    y = iota&#xA;    z = &amp;#34;zz&amp;#34;&#xA;    k = &amp;#34;zz&amp;#34;&#xA;    p = iota&#xA;)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;iota&lt;/code&gt; is equivalent to the line index of the &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt; block.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
